      "index": "b1P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1795309276,
      "version": 34,
      "versionNonce": 2129325065,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791218801720,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• You set a min ↔ max NODE range for the pool\n• Fabric adds nodes as tasks queue up behind current\nexecutors, and removes nodes once they sit idle\n  (spark.yarn.executor.decommission.\n  enabled = true by default)\n• Scaling reacts to the CURRENT session's own\nworkload only — it doesn't borrow nodes from, or lend\nnodes to, other concurrent sessions\n• Node SIZE (vCores/node) is fixed once chosen — only\nthe node COUNT scales up and down",
      "fontSize": 14.5,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• You set a min ↔ max NODE range for the pool\n• Fabric adds nodes as tasks queue up behind current executors, and removes nodes once they sit idle\n  (spark.yarn.executor.decommission.\n  enabled = true by default)\n• Scaling reacts to the CURRENT session's own workload only — it doesn't borrow nodes from, or lend nodes to, other concurrent sessions\n• Node SIZE (vCores/node) is fixed once chosen — only the node COUNT scales up and down",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
